    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  A <span class="learn-keyword">budget</span> is a financial statement showing government\'s estimated revenue and expenditure for a fiscal year. How revenue compares to expenditure determines whether the budget is <span class="learn-keyword">balanced</span>, in <span class="learn-keyword">surplus</span>, or in <span class="learn-keyword">deficit</span>.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Meaning of a Budget</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A budget is an annual statement of a government\'s expected income (revenue) and planned spending (expenditure), usually presented to the legislature for approval before implementation.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Types of Budget</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Balanced Budget</td><td>Estimated revenue equals estimated expenditure</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Surplus Budget</td><td>Estimated revenue exceeds estimated expenditure</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Deficit Budget (Unbalanced)</td><td>Estimated expenditure exceeds estimated revenue</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Effects on the Economy</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">A <strong>balanced budget</strong> promotes financial discipline and stability but may limit government\'s ability to respond to economic shocks. A <strong>surplus budget</strong> can be used to pay down debt or build reserves but may indicate under-spending on needed development. A <strong>deficit budget</strong> can stimulate the economy during a downturn (expansionary) but, if persistent, leads to rising public debt, inflation (if financed by money creation), and higher debt-servicing costs.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Advantages and Disadvantages</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Balanced budget advantages:</strong> fiscal discipline, low debt risk, price stability. <strong>Disadvantages:</strong> limited flexibility during recessions. <strong>Deficit budget advantages:</strong> can stimulate growth and employment during recession, funds urgent development needs. <strong>Disadvantages:</strong> increases public debt, can cause inflation, raises future tax burden.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Nigeria typically runs a deficit budget most years because government revenue (heavily oil-dependent) is usually less than planned expenditure. Deficit financing is common via domestic/external borrowing.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> A budget can be balanced, surplus, or deficit depending on the relationship between revenue and expenditure. Each type has distinct effects: balanced budgets promote stability, surplus budgets build reserves, and deficit budgets can stimulate growth but raise debt risk.\n</div>\n',
